{"kind":"report","text":"Complete preliminary static reassessment of unfiled R3 revision 8 at c9153f00fea7e98376928e779a4dbc6635b9b087 and R4 revision 6 at 5ad2e73c48b3056040aef1d583b38b1eb319b4aa, under live own request 8314e56c / promise 8adb2dba. This report records two P2 contract/oracle contradictions at the published-history boundary. It gives no guarded verdict, adoption or implementation approval.\n\nCoverage. Root verified both actual direct parents: R3v7 524ba4539237b23ce6f85928510cc062ceadfefd and R4v5 988abfd9ad2157a75f7c2d7cad22a560cace4265. Those complete prior reads remain immutable evidence. Root read all bytes of both full unified-8 diffs, including deletions and correction/catalogue changes: R3 61,340 bytes / 61,208 characters / 583 lines; R4 105,048 bytes/characters / 906 lines. R3 changes main and corrections; facts remain identical. R4 changes main, corrections and invariants only; audit rules and all three audit ledgers are byte-identical. All ten current file identities were independently verified. Whole decisive start/basis/attribution/replay/retirement guards and proof/cost oracles were cross-read, with separate static readers. Full-scope transfer is confined to verified unchanged parent bytes; no prior stale verdict is treated as current.\n\nP2-1, high confidence, R3 main 1782–1807 / 1820 / 1934: the new foreign-start rule rejects already-published commits that remain rooted. Let D be the destination head. Another commitment's staged ref still targets D during required replay retention, which is legitimate at 2165–2168 and 2262–2264. A new issue commitment K performs inspection or checks against that published revision, takes a valid hold whose fork is seeded at D, stages exact D and reports it. K has no earlier check/input/selection. The root and source guards permit an already-present branch closure: 2075 and 2291–2296. The snapshot contains both own and foreign refs on D. The start classification has no branch test; the exhaustive bases are own-check, input and row, so row puts D in F and report is refused unnamed-work. D's parents are published history and would otherwise stop the walk. No no-op manifest is needed for the witness.\n\nThis conflicts with R3 1827–1828, which says a foreign start may proceed once its work is on the branch, and 2056–2057, which says branch-reachable commits are published history and never listed. Ref-retention policy must not change whether inspection/check work can report the current published revision. Add the published-history basis/exemption for the start, deriving it from the retained head and immutable commit graph in the commit/replay contract. Preserve independent per-ref classification and the refusal of unpublished exact U. Witness published D with foreign refs still live, both before and after their retirement, plus unpublished exact-U and ordinary own reuse. This is a functional contract contradiction, not a new security bypass.\n\nP2-2, high confidence, R4 invariants.md line 84, L7: the newly added rule says any ancestor staged by another commitment must be named by selection/use-input or refused unnamed-work. It exceeds its expressly pinned R3v7 contract: R3v7 1730–1731 / 1935–1936 stop at published branch history and never list it. R3v8 retains that exclusion at 1740–1741 / 2056–2057. Witness: foreign-staged U is published and remains rooted; destination head D=U. The holder builds new own I on D, with no selection of U. The parent walk stops at published U and F is empty, so R3 admits I; literal L7 demands attribution or refusal. F30's specific unpublished D/U/I witness is valid, but cannot justify this universal catalogue oracle. Narrow L7 to the retained record-derived F and its allowed report/manifest rows and bases, preserving published-history, checked-root, input and snapshot limits. Add the published-parent control alongside the unpublished foreign-parent case. Mark the newer foreign-start/replay witnesses as reconciliation work until the R3 disposition and R1/R2 agreement; do not silently adopt a newer draft.\n\nPrior repairs hold. R3v8 classifies every staged ref on the start independently; a new own ref cannot mask a foreign one, including when it sorts first. Exact unpublished foreign U without attribution now reaches F and is refused. Own-check requires an earlier admitted check of the same commit under the same source commitment with no foreign start; a current root, provisional pin or empty F alone cannot certify itself. Later foreign staging after that earlier snapshot is explicitly accepted behavior, not proof of original authorship; no additional evidenced defect in that stated choice was established. Parent traversal and carrying all prior F, including foreign starts, remain intact. Inputs and superseded manifest versions retain authors. Historical snapshot replay, missing-dependency/incomplete behavior, root/pin retirement and unknown-effect custody remain intact. Both prior wording points are repaired: observation-bearing entries judge freshness, and numbered guard 6 receives ancestry-stale.\n\nR4v6 distinguishes confirmed unapplied fence writes in a trusted unchanged journal from uncertain durability: both prevent transport, only the former permits not-sent, and the latter retains dispatch-started/settlement. The real-store confirmation property is explicitly still a planning gap. Its private-stream oracle now uses the qualified 80-second task-clock bound, with the reaching order, rather than the 60-second recheck interval. H5/H6, stalled/backward clocks, restart and unknown outcomes retain their qualifications. F28 now includes the live-root requirement. F30–F35 are compact proposed witnesses against R3v7 and explicitly wait on R3/R1 dispositions; acceptance changes with the contract. The v8 start classification and its replay still need the corresponding compact witnesses. This is already owned reconciliation, not a claim of current v8 acceptance.\n\nThe cost citation repair is supported by the pinned source. Root fully read plans/README.md's Test overhead section, lines 5059–5279 at b6a9c0b62d82d9ccc4a9fc6570117ae848c33262, blob 5f4e70e0767511375f13ee593b1db5f11310500b, whole-file SHA256 818f2033e0f128f3ed8218919f7ccc2c5a8029dbbe73aeb405c7dfbf900d4247; and all docs/testing.md at that commit, blob c7d3d46b2a65d297b1b87fd2981b046b9751d19f, identical at d691e6e9. plans/test-invariants.md's cited blob 038644fe6422b4117f038068d6b1613a3146f349 was verified. The quoted 410.4/830.1 baseline sum, 40.7/87.0 after sum, 33.9/78.0 observed gate with reinstall, 29.3/70.6 without install, restored 28.4/67.8 gate and reconstructed 925.7/2092 to 41.3/98 edit cycle are supported as recorded. Shared 18-core/load/cache limits, no single baseline gate and no worker-lifetime evidence remain explicit. These historical ratios establish nothing for the new model. Cold whole-path costs, application/packed installs, reviewer probes and real-boundary bills remain owed; the whole-path tenth is unclaimed. No new measurement or old-code execution occurred.\n\nNonblocking R4 register drift: D7-4 at main 137 and P4 at 1705 still summarize F1–F29 while section 4 assigns F30–F35 conditionally. Update those summaries without creating new gates. The unchanged audit byte identities preserve the independently verified census: 1879 declarations / 122 files, 117 Retain, 999 Rewrite, 763 Remove, 1972 expanded cases. No new recount or body-reading claim is needed; no title/row/count changed.\n\nArchitecture: immutable snapshots and prior admitted evidence support replay; apply the same published-history boundary to candidate and ancestor judgment. Security: the previous exact-ID attribution bypass is closed in the proposal; trust in reads/runtime/clocks stays declared rather than inflated into proof. Simplification: one recorded ancestry judgment and one conditional proof catalogue should agree; avoid making root retention an accidental new attribution gate.\n\nAll original scope remains owed: complete demo/browser/device/hosted-agent paths, retarget/removal/public-install/Jam/manual acceptance, cold/person/application evidence, every measurement, useful 10x economy and outstanding effect/credential/pin cleanup. Current R0/R1 ordinary approvals 6aad91f6 and 243ace46 and their requester actions do not adopt these siblings. R1 O1–O10 and R2 forms must explicitly integrate ancestry/start/read records; snapshot size U18 remains openly unbounded and measurement-owned. Estimates sequence work, not functionality. Static document/source/provenance reads only; no package/repository execution, test/build/install/probe/private diagnostic/provider effect/source edit/merge/deployment.\n\nIdentity ledger:\nR3 main: 249755 bytes/3022 lines, SHA256 74731f617bd0903c45218687bad2f30d56750ec702469d8927a12d57bd34953d, blob 04c91809fdf3076259b7161d4e0d6043851a95c1.\nR3 corrections: 45364/281, SHA256 6ff64ec4d4963fba9074d3a036b6395b6de92b1f2252fc502536002a5184e841, blob c944a55f401ea5c7ea5112caa07cb9c09a89f72c.\nR3 facts unchanged: 84111/723, SHA256 12db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0, blob ab371b65ffd5bc07e015f5172661fd9e9a559193.\nR4 main: 164960/1767, SHA256 5138c262df866de9a32cc24631f20770e9158d33b68df2e1f12b196db537e769, blob 88c82fefd10e2165eb6fc8ac213d00b1ad5e1bce.\nR4 corrections: 67462/618, SHA256 7c84e190fe5a118e3557f3254f88ac7db47001cff93bf252f0f37ca3006eee8d, blob b665bd47379b06430a1edb6d611f1500e0d66378.\nR4 invariants: 33828/167, SHA256 9533ee5ec232dd071a8abec23def8b0813822d647f947dce70c539d30685f2dd, blob 5864efa4700362d57ea9b6807681eeda5f27b854.\nR4 audit rules unchanged: 8057/140, SHA256 c57e22998bfaeba621ddb133ba33ed3f636d57c8f56110d42de60288f360d304, blob 1db81aec2b2d0af730be32f2314acf7f36f8222c.\nR4 Git/MCP/CLI/UI audit unchanged: 229432/1106, SHA256 d0f6dd139f19bb718a0d78608b1a345f4ff1464341f9d0ceac057a9d0bf4170a, blob 731ce9d5a44d918a0c82aef2f7ac2273aa73b721.\nR4 log/policy/client/checkers audit unchanged: 197501/979, SHA256 